    "image_with_text_VWezQh": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_pT6AFx": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Nuclear Industry"
          }
        },
        "heading_7KRGth": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why are adhesive tapes and labels used for nuclear applications?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h4"
          }
        },
        "text_iXGwGp": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Adhesive tapes and labels enhance the safety and efficiency of a variety of nuclear applications, including:</p><ul><li><strong>Contamination Control: </strong>Nuclear tape is used to reduce the potential for contamination in processes that involve radioactive materials. They are used to seal ducts and lines, cover openings, and affix instructions and warning labels to facilitate safe operations.</li><li><strong>Corrosion Resistance: </strong>Nuclear tapes are applied to the surface of sensitive pipes, connections, and other components in nuclear applications to prevent damage from corrosion or abrasion.</li><li><strong>General Adhesion:</strong> Nuclear adhesive tapes are also used for general adhesive applications such as minor repairs and fixes, hanging general signage, and securing protective gear.</li><li><strong>Safety Precautions: </strong>In nuclear applications, safety is paramount. That’s why nuclear tapes and labels are critical to ensure that workers avoid hazardous areas and know to wear the appropriate protective equipment. In addition, they help to prevent radioactive exposure by clearly identifying the presence of radioactive components and equipment while they are being used, stored, or shipped.</li><li><strong>Testing and Cleanup Equipment: </strong>Tapes and labels are used in RAD smear and wipe test kits to provide clear identification and instructions for safe, reliable testing and spill cleanup.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "subheading_pT6AFx",
        "heading_7KRGth",
        "text_iXGwGp"
      ],
